<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">El Atteuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1012</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">El Atteuf is the oldest of the five fortified towns of the Mzab valley in the Algerian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, founded by Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> around 1012. Its houses climb a hill around the mosque in the compact style of the valley. Its Sidi Brahim mosque influenced the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-corbusier">Le Corbusier</a>, and the town is part of the M'zab Valley World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/el-atteuf.jpg" alt="El Atteuf" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stefan Krasowski from New York, NY, USA · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El-Atteuf_Ghardaia_Algeria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
